{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Arial;}}\fs32\b Hypothetical training example\b0\par\fs24\b Hypothetical Login Defect: Password Field Has No Visible Validation Feedback When Submitted Empty\b0\par\par\fs22\b Environment\b0\par\fs18 Application: https://app.vwo.com/\par\fs18 Browser: Not supplied\par\fs18 Browser version: Not supplied\par\fs18 Operating system: Not supplied\par\fs18 Build: Not supplied\par\fs18 Execution time: Not supplied\par\par\fs22\b Preconditions\b0\par\fs18 1. The user is logged out.\par\fs18 2. An active registered test account is available.\par\fs18 3. The login page is accessible.\par\par\fs22\b Test Data\b0\par\fs18 Registered email: <registered_email>\par\fs18 Password: <empty>\par\par\fs22\b Steps to Reproduce\b0\par\fs18 1. Open https://app.vwo.com/.\par\fs18 2. Enter a registered test email in the email field.\par\fs18 3. Leave the password field empty.\par\fs18 4. Submit the login form.\par\par\fs22\b Expected Result\b0\par\fs18 Because password is a mandatory field, login must not succeed with an empty password. The form should provide visible feedback indicating that the password is required, or otherwise prevent submission. The exact validation message is not specified and must not be assumed.\par\par\fs22\b Actual Result\b0\par\fs18 Observed: The form submits after the password is left empty, and no visible validation feedback appears. The dashboard state after submission is not supplied. Assumption: This observation alone does not confirm whether authentication succeeds; that outcome requires execution and evidence.\par\par\fs22\b Reproducibility\b0\par\fs18 3 out of 3 attempts.\par\par\fs22\b Suggested Severity and rationale\b0\par\fs18 Provisional severity: Medium-High. Rationale: The mandatory-password control is not providing visible feedback, which may permit or obscure an invalid submission. If testing confirms that login succeeds or protected dashboard access is granted with an empty password, severity should be raised. This is provisional until browser, build, session state, and evidence are supplied.\par\par\fs22\b Attachments\b0\par\fs18 Not provided.\par\par}